WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.500
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
ima wa ugokenai sore ga sadame dakedo

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
Right now I can't move... That is my fate, but...

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
akirame wa shinai mou mezameta kara

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
I won't give up anymore because I have awakened.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
moeru tokimeki wa jidai wo utsushi

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
My burning, throbbing heart reflects the era...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
iro azayaka ni moesakaru honoo

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
It has the color of vividly blazing flames...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying ima wa mienaku tomo

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying, though I can't see it right now...

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching michi shirube wa ukabu

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching, a guidepost floats up ahead.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.170
I wanna have a pure time!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.280
Everyone's a noble mind!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
soko ni nokotta wakasa toridashi

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
I'll take out what remains of my youth there,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.980
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.540
beyond the hard times from now!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
kawaku kuchibiru nureteiru nara

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
If these dry lips become wet,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
toki wo norikoe atsui jidai e to

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
Beyond time, towards a passionate era,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
utsuru darou to shinjiteiru kara

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
Because I believe it will move...

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.060
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.690
beyond the hard times from now...

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:43.980
The Republic of Zeon was considered
a local autonomous body...

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:46.320
...of the Earth Federation Government.

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:49.920
However, in concert with the actions
of the Titans...

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.730
...they had begun taking actions
on their own.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:56.290
High-ranking officials of the
Earth Federation Government...

00:01:56.370 --> 00:02:01.330
...had overlooked this mainly because
they had little interest in outer space.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:10.050
Amuro Flies Again

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:32.530
<i>The course is clear. You may take off!</i>

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:34.570
Rosamia squad, taking off!

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:55.160
<i>The Audhumla is presently proceeding</i>
<i>north-northwest!</i>

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:56.660
Roger!

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:59.390
We estimate encounter with the enemy
in fifty minutes.

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:01.060
Requesting contact with Major Buran.

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:10.160
I recall there being a Titans establishment
in this area.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:13.170
Sure there is, since this is where
the United States used to be.

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:15.150
You'll find numerous
military establishments on this.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:16.180
Hmm...!

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.310
- Please.
- Yes, sir!

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:21.750
Assuming the troops who attacked us
at Kennedy Spaceport...

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:22.750
...came after us on the Sudori...!

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:24.650
It would take them at least half a day.

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:26.190
It won't take them that long.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:29.160
Kamille, have the Mk. II ready
to send out on short notice!

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:32.960
Lieutenant, doesn't it bother you at all
that Lt. Roberto was killed in action?!

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:35.300
You want to return to space, don't you?

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:36.430
W-Well, sure...!

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:39.830
What we can do for Lt. Roberto right now
is to return to space.

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:41.230
Forget your sentiments in war!

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.140
A message from the relay station!

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:47.610
Reinforcements are headed our way!

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.470
They plan to join us in forty minutes!

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:53.640
Who's the combat leader?

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:55.520
Someone called Ensign Rosamia Badam.

00:03:56.020 --> 00:04:00.120
Oh, right.
Rosamia from the Augusta Lab.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:01.780
Is it okay to have her?

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:05.300
Well, with her we already know
we'll come out on top.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:10.430
But with the outcome so predictable,
the game loses its excitement.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:16.840
I couldn't do much for you...

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:20.740
...but if there's anything that worries you,
don't hesitate to contact me anytime.

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:22.540
We won't ever be bothering you again!

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:25.210
We can make it on our own!

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:27.110
I hope you have a healthy baby, Fraw Bow.

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:28.620
Thank you.

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:30.480
I'll need to raise this child to be strong.

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:33.260
You're right.

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:36.660
It's almost time.

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:38.790
Let's move to the seats inside.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:42.490
What more do you expect me to do?!

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.000
It wasn't easy to get those tickets to Japan!

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:48.660
I know I'm being watched even as I speak.

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:50.940
They'd capture me before I could do anything!

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:52.280
Amuro...!

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:53.740
Captain!

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:58.410
Remember that you're not going to gain
anything by trying to become a child again.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:04:59.450
Fraw!

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:09.820
A freighter.

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:23.530
Katz, do you know where Hayato...
your father is?

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:25.930
I don't know.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:28.170
He left to help the A.E.U.G. at Jaburo.

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:31.450
If we can make it to Kennedy,
will we have an idea of the situation?

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:33.250
Sure, since there are Karaba crew there.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:37.520
But it may be in ruins from being attacked
by the Earth Federation Forces.

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:38.860
Fraw.

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:41.420
Do you mind if I borrow Katz for a while?

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:42.460
Amuro?

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:45.060
Then I'll go, too!

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:46.530
No.

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:49.660
You two must protect your mother.
Especially with the baby on its way.

00:05:50.170 --> 00:05:51.100
Mr. Amuro's right.

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:53.100
You guys go on to Japan.

00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:55.670
And once the baby is born...

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:57.670
...get a Colony-bound ticket
from New Hong Kong.

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:01.510
<i>Flight 308 is now boarding passengers.</i>
<i>Will passengers kindly make...</i>

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:04.480
- <i>...their way to the boarding gate?</i>
- Take care of Mother, okay?

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:05.740
But how are you going to...?

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:09.620
As long as you let me borrow Katz,
we men will deal with the rest.

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:12.420
You mustn't worry about it, Fraw.

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:14.580
Amuro, are you serious?

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:19.400
Goodbye, Fraw.

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:22.090
- Don't you need to go to the bathroom?
- I do, Pop.

00:06:22.170 --> 00:06:23.360
Cheeky boy!

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:37.670
We'll dash to the top
of that freighter's ladder!

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:38.650
Yes!

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:57.960
Close the hatch!

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:07.710
<i>We will be taking off</i>
<i>according to schedule.</i>

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:12.240
<i>Please check again that your seatbelt</i>
<i>is securely fastened.</i>

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:15.650
What?!

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:31.530
- We stopped!
- <i>Please wait for a moment...</i>

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:33.470
<i>...while a military plane</i>
<i>makes an emergency take-off.</i>

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:35.130
Worried?

00:07:35.210 --> 00:07:36.830
A little.

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:40.930
But... only a little.

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:46.240
We're taking off!

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:48.380
But this isn't a runway!

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:51.890
We have the distance! I don't want to
get in the way of Fraw's passenger plane!

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:13.000
<i>We're sorry to have kept you waiting.</i>

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:15.010
Have a safe trip!

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:17.280
Stop that passenger plane!
Flight 308!

00:08:33.100 --> 00:08:34.830
- Wear this.
- Yes.

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:55.850
It's as we estimated. The Sudori.

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:56.780
No, it isn't!

00:08:57.890 --> 00:08:59.620
That's not Major Buran Blutarch's aircraft.

00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:06.350
Is it the A.E.U.G.'s Garuda
that took off from Kennedy Spaceport?

00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:16.430
Director Hayato.

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:18.810
I thought I saw aircraft shadows below.

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:20.440
There are more residences in this area.

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:23.310
Confirm it. It's an area where civilians
are also flying planes.

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:26.110
Shall we have Lieutenant Quattro's
mobile suit unit on standby?

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:27.880
Get them ready!

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:31.680
Are we battling in this populated area?

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:33.280
All units, get ready!

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:39.020
As I thought. Damn A.E.U.G.!
Choosing this place!

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:41.000
Ignore the mobile suits if they come out!

00:09:41.070 --> 00:09:42.400
Our priority is to shoot down the Garuda!

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:45.840
<i>Wait! You'll attack from within!</i>

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:52.770
Despite what he's saying,
I wonder if he actually loves war!

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:57.510
<i>Weren't you listening</i>
<i>to Lieutenant Quattro's orders?!</i>

00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:59.380
<i>Don't leave the Audhumla!</i>

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:00.420
What?

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:02.950
<i>Didn't you hear?!</i>
<i>We're attacking from here!</i>

00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:03.990
Roger!

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:14.260
I'm going to head straight into them.
Everyone else, keep that mobile suit back!

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:25.640
That mobile suit's flying on its own!

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:28.680
A mobile armor?!

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:35.350
It's a mobile armor!

00:10:35.420 --> 00:10:38.360
- We'll send out our mobile suits!
- <i>It's too late for that!</i>

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:39.690
Damn Kamille!

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:46.130
I'm falling!

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:49.930
We lost one?!

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:03.340
Damage incurred!

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:06.350
This doesn't even count as being hit!
Calm down!

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:09.390
- But we could crash into a residential area!
- There's no way we'll crash!

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:13.520
At this rate, we're practically waiting
to be struck down!

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:22.260
The clouds aren't that thick.

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:23.730
I'll just wait it out!

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:29.300
- Open the fore hatch!
- <i>But!</i>

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:32.210
I'm not about to be struck down
while stuck within the Audhumla!

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:32.870
<i>Roger!</i>

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:39.750
I'm not going to be defeated that easily!

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:44.680
A mobile suit?!

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:52.230
A mobile suit on a sled
is no match for this Gaplant!

00:11:54.370 --> 00:11:55.630
Not letting you!

00:12:13.050 --> 00:12:13.880
You're going to die!

00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:17.690
What?!

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:26.690
It's because you indiscriminately open fire
in a place like this!

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:28.250
I'll crush you!

00:12:30.230 --> 00:12:32.100
Kamille is out there engaged in a battle!

00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:33.360
Bastard!

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:36.030
Kamille's left? Where is he?

00:12:39.510 --> 00:12:42.340
What fool thinks about
where they're fighting during a battle?

00:12:42.410 --> 00:12:43.680
Who is this dimwit?!

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:45.580
You calling me a dimwit?!

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:47.620
Hurry up and crush me!

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:48.520
I lose.

00:12:48.890 --> 00:12:49.680
What did you say?

00:12:56.230 --> 00:12:56.960
What?!

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:05.430
Stop talking like some child!

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:20.650
Mine moves a lot better
in battles even while descending!

00:13:23.890 --> 00:13:26.720
My shield! There's my Dodai!

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:35.460
I told you, I've got the superior mobility!

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:42.100
I got you!

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:43.040
<i>Go down!</i>

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:46.070
Go down!!

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:53.810
I never knew mobile suits like that existed!

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:54.650
Well, now we know!

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:57.650
- But it's retreating!
- G-Good!

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:02.230
I got carried away
and moved about too much.

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:04.660
I'll need to join the Sudori
before this runs out of power!

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:15.610
What a quick switch.

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:16.660
Kamille.

00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:19.510
Did he receive permission
from Director Hayato for his sortie?

00:14:27.020 --> 00:14:28.990
Are you going to "correct" me?

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:34.090
I don't think simply hitting you
would improve your personality.

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:37.760
I do realize that I was saved
by Lieutenant Quattro.

00:14:38.330 --> 00:14:42.130
I'm glad to hear you at least realized that
amidst a battle.

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:43.390
You'd better be grateful.

00:14:43.470 --> 00:14:44.490
Yes.

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:46.540
But Director Hayato, that's not all.

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:50.710
I was being pulled by that
transforming mobile suit.

00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:54.440
Are you making excuses?!

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:56.040
No, sir.

00:14:56.110 --> 00:14:57.580
Excuse me, Director Hayato.

00:14:57.820 --> 00:15:00.440
I can verify what Kamille just said.

00:15:03.860 --> 00:15:06.290
Then I shall hold back this fist.

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:10.450
We came across a mobile armor
back when we rescued Captain Bright.

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:13.760
This one was very similar.
Wasn't it, Kamille?

00:15:14.070 --> 00:15:16.930
Yes, I felt great danger.

00:15:37.720 --> 00:15:40.420
Thank you for bringing us in.

00:15:40.490 --> 00:15:41.720
It couldn't be helped.

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:44.020
You're obviously not used to operating
the Gaplant.

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:45.820
I suggest you get used to it
through this operation.

00:15:46.330 --> 00:15:47.230
Yes, sir.

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:49.700
However, you've helped out
by delaying the Audhumla.

00:15:50.270 --> 00:15:52.000
I'll send out a second wave immediately.

00:15:52.670 --> 00:15:54.730
They wouldn't dream of a second attack
right away.

00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:55.670
No, sir.

00:15:55.740 --> 00:15:57.640
Use my people for your repairs.

00:15:57.710 --> 00:15:59.800
I've sent a crew out
to retrieve your booster.

00:15:59.880 --> 00:16:02.070
Thank you very much.

00:16:05.720 --> 00:16:07.950
Don't you have difficulty breathing
at this high altitude?

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:10.680
My lungs have been enhanced, sir.

00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:12.220
I'm all right.

00:16:12.290 --> 00:16:13.590
That's good to hear.

00:16:19.930 --> 00:16:21.520
Rosamia Badam.

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:24.570
She seems to be almost manifesting
the abilities expected of her.

00:16:24.640 --> 00:16:26.690
Has she successfully become
a Cyber-Newtype?

00:16:29.310 --> 00:16:30.270
I'm going!

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:51.660
It could be the guy from earlier!

00:16:51.730 --> 00:16:54.930
It's dangerous to confront them alone.
We'll strike from both sides.

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:56.400
Yes, Lieutenant!

00:16:56.470 --> 00:16:57.730
Okay!

00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:00.770
Another enemy attack!

00:17:00.840 --> 00:17:02.700
That's right!
The same guys that attacked Kennedy!

00:17:02.770 --> 00:17:04.260
They're back too soon!

00:17:11.120 --> 00:17:12.510
I won't allow it.

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:22.780
Enemy locked on!

00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:29.730
They've got us?

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:31.230
Director Hayato! Increase altitude!

00:17:36.710 --> 00:17:38.110
What's that?

00:17:38.180 --> 00:17:40.610
So, those flashes were from a battle
after all.

00:17:40.980 --> 00:17:42.610
<i>Here we go, Lieutenant Quattro!</i>

00:17:43.180 --> 00:17:44.580
That's Father's voice.

00:17:44.650 --> 00:17:45.780
He's on that!

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:48.450
Space aliens would've been better off
staying in space!

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:07.540
Kamille, don't let it get above!

00:18:07.610 --> 00:18:08.900
We've got our limits.

00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:11.240
<i>Roger, I'll go around its right.</i>

00:18:29.090 --> 00:18:30.890
No matter what!

00:18:32.600 --> 00:18:34.150
I'm taking that mobile suit down.

00:18:34.230 --> 00:18:35.130
Mr. Amuro?

00:18:35.200 --> 00:18:36.790
Katz, escape on the Homo Avis!

00:18:36.870 --> 00:18:37.890
- Hurry!
- Y-Yes!

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:53.380
Cartridge!

00:18:56.050 --> 00:18:56.780
Right there!

00:18:58.290 --> 00:18:59.220
You won't hit me!

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:07.860
That's the best you'll do
with the scatter shots!

00:19:18.510 --> 00:19:19.770
What's that freighter doing there?

00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:33.150
I'll end up hitting the Audhumla!

00:19:34.930 --> 00:19:35.860
What's going on?!

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:39.690
What are you up to, Amuro?

00:19:40.730 --> 00:19:41.660
Amuro...?!

00:19:42.100 --> 00:19:43.400
Stay back, Char!

00:19:45.800 --> 00:19:47.740
You're going down, A.E.U.G.!

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:49.770
Damn!

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:55.400
What?!

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:19.300
All units, retreat!

00:20:30.180 --> 00:20:31.110
There's a person!

00:21:00.640 --> 00:21:04.080
A Gundam... Mk. II...!

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:17.430
I've never seen that mobile suit before.

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:20.360
Is it one of the A.E.U.G.'s new models?

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:32.000
Amuro...!

00:21:38.820 --> 00:21:39.840
That's Amuro Ray...!

00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:49.020
I said Char...

00:21:49.390 --> 00:21:50.190
...didn't I?

00:21:52.530 --> 00:21:53.590
I hope you're okay.

00:21:54.230 --> 00:21:56.200
I'm fine, thank you.

00:22:04.640 --> 00:22:05.700
That's Char.

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:08.740
However...!

00:22:16.750 --> 00:22:18.720
No question about it.

00:22:19.420 --> 00:22:20.480
That's Amuro Ray.

00:22:22.560 --> 00:22:23.420
Char...!

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:45.350 --> 00:23:50.550
Just before the Audhumla reaches Hickory,
Rosamia's Gaplant intercepts it.

00:23:50.760 --> 00:23:55.890
Katz dashes out to face this,
motivated by Amuro's indecisiveness.

00:23:56.560 --> 00:24:02.020
Kamille and Char take off to rescue
the Gundam Mk. II, piloted by Katz.

00:24:02.100 --> 00:24:07.440
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"Katz's Sortie".

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Next Episode

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Katz's Sortie

00:24:07.910 --> 00:24:10.540
You will see the tears of time.
